Yeah.

971
00:41:36.800 --> 00:41:38.120
Don't worry about it.

972
00:41:38.800 --> 00:41:40.300
It doesn't involve you.

973
00:41:40.500 --> 00:41:41.220
We got it covered.

974
00:41:41.520 --> 00:41:46.060
They're discussing a room with a view and who walks in but Andy.

975
00:41:46.420 --> 00:41:47.780
He wants to be in the club.

976
00:41:48.000 --> 00:41:51.020
And Pam tells him it's a closed club.

977
00:41:51.800 --> 00:41:56.260
She's very direct and unapologetic.

978
00:41:56.260 --> 00:41:57.040
I'm sorry.

979
00:41:57.280 --> 00:41:58.680
This is a closed club.

980
00:41:59.020 --> 00:42:05.380
And Andy has a talking head where he says the Finer Things Club is the most exclusive club in the office.

981
00:42:05.520 --> 00:42:07.600
So it's naturally where he needs to be.

982
00:42:08.320 --> 00:42:10.600
Party planning committee is his backup.

983
00:42:11.200 --> 00:42:12.600
Kevin's band is his safety.

984
00:42:14.160 --> 00:42:16.380
Everything is like he's rushing a fraternity.

985
00:42:16.720 --> 00:42:17.940
It's so true.

986
00:42:18.280 --> 00:42:19.260
It's so true.

987
00:42:19.260 --> 00:42:22.640
Well, I'll have you know, we loved shooting these scenes.

988
00:42:22.900 --> 00:42:24.560
Me, Oscar, Paul.

989
00:42:24.800 --> 00:42:26.640
We were delighted by the storyline.

990
00:42:26.900 --> 00:42:31.180
We had the best time because this was a group of people that did not normally get to hang out.

991
00:42:31.340 --> 00:42:33.680
I did not have a lot of scenes with Oscar or Paul.

992
00:42:33.800 --> 00:42:35.420
So this was really cool.

